// English translations of archive descriptions, records 321–483. Source wording and qualifications are retained.
Object.assign(window.NUO_EN = window.NUO_EN || {}, {
  "萍乡湘东傩面具系列中的金花， 金花人生暂无相信介绍。该面具为江西萍乡湘东傩戏或傩仪中的角色面具，主要用于仪式表演、迎神还愿或民间信仰叙事。": "Jinhua from the Xiangdong Nuo mask series, Pingxiang. No detailed biography is provided. This is a character mask associated with Nuo drama or ritual in Xiangdong, Pingxiang, Jiangxi, used in ritual performance, welcoming deities, fulfilling vows or narratives of popular belief.",
  "萍乡湘东傩面具系列中的土地神， 土地神，也叫福德正神，是管理一方的社神。秦汉以后为民俗广泛祀奉。在道教神系中地位较低，但在民间信仰极为普遍。": "Tudi, the Earth God, from the Xiangdong Nuo mask series, Pingxiang. Also called Fude Zhengshen, he oversees the land of a local community. His worship became widespread after the Qin and Han periods. Though relatively low in the Daoist hierarchy, he is extremely common in popular religion.",
  "萍乡湘东傩面具系列中的吞口， 吞口往往安放于宅门首、畜圈旁、寨门口，其目的是以辟邪消灾，保人畜平安。": "Tunkou from the Xiangdong Nuo mask series, Pingxiang. Tunkou are often placed above house entrances, beside livestock pens or at village gates to ward off misfortune and protect people and animals.",
  "萍乡湘东傩面具系列中的唐将军“古傩迎宾”， 创作历程：“这就是唐将军，我给取了名叫做‘古傩迎宾’。”彭国龙一脸虔诚地说，箱里的唐将军傩面具是他从事傩雕以来花费心血最多、耗费时间最长的古傩面具。“我用了整整两个月的时间才完成。”彭国龙轻抚着面具说，傩雕的工艺很繁杂，要想成为一名好的傩雕师，就一定要耐得住寂寞。": "General Tang, titled Ancient Nuo Welcomes Guests, from the Xiangdong Nuo mask series, Pingxiang. Peng Guolong named this work himself. He described it as the traditional Nuo mask into which he had put the most effort and time since becoming a carver: it took two full months to complete. As he gently touched the mask, he explained that Nuo carving involves complex techniques and requires a craftsperson to be comfortable working patiently in solitude.",
  "萍乡湘东傩面具系列中的龙王， 龙王是古代神话传说中在水里统领水族的王，掌管兴云降雨。传说龙能行云布雨、消灾降福，象征祥瑞，所以以舞龙的方式来祈求平安和丰收就成为全国民间各地的一种习俗。": "The Dragon King from the Xiangdong Nuo mask series, Pingxiang. In traditional mythology, the Dragon King rules aquatic creatures and governs clouds and rain. Dragons are believed to bring rain, avert misfortune and bestow blessings, making them auspicious symbols. Dragon dances to pray for peace and good harvests became a widespread folk custom.",
  "萍乡湘东傩面具系列中的钟馗， 钟馗时道教俗神，专司打鬼驱邪。中国民间常挂钟馗神像辟邪除灾，从古至今都流传着“钟馗捉鬼的典故传说。": "Zhong Kui from the Xiangdong Nuo mask series, Pingxiang. Zhong Kui is a popular Daoist deity who catches ghosts and drives away evil. Images of him are hung to avert misfortune, and stories of Zhong Kui catching ghosts have circulated for centuries.",
  "萍乡湘东傩面具系列中的武财神， 武财神是中国民间信仰的一类财神。武财神的由来和职能：财神有文财神和武财神之区分，文财神是比干、范蠡和李诡祖，武财神是关羽、柴荣和赵公明。关帝阁的武财神关羽手持青龙偃月刀，形象威武，义薄云天。赵公明一手拿元宝，一手拿长鞭。": "The Martial God of Wealth from the Xiangdong Nuo mask series, Pingxiang. Popular religion distinguishes civil and martial wealth deities. The civil group includes Bi Gan, Fan Li and Li Guizu; the martial group includes Guan Yu, Chai Rong and Zhao Gongming. Guan Yu at Guandi Pavilion carries the Green Dragon Crescent Blade and is portrayed as mighty and righteous. Zhao Gongming holds an ingot in one hand and a long whip in the other.",
  "萍乡湘东傩面具系列中的小鬼， 小鬼原意指阴间地位低下的鬼，出自《史记·封禅书》，后指鬼神的差使。": "The Little Ghost from the Xiangdong Nuo mask series, Pingxiang. The term originally referred to a low-ranking underworld ghost, appearing in the Treatise on the Feng and Shan Sacrifices in the Records of the Grand Historian. It later referred to an attendant serving spirits or deities.",
  "萍乡湘东傩面具系列中的马将军。该面具表现历史、小说或民间戏曲中的武将人物，通常用于突出忠勇、威严或护卫性的角色身份。": "General Ma from the Xiangdong Nuo mask series, Pingxiang. The mask portrays a military figure from history, fiction or folk drama, emphasizing loyalty, courage, authority or a protective role.",
  "萍乡湘东傩面具系列中的五方将（东）。该面具为江西萍乡湘东傩戏或傩仪中的角色面具，主要用于仪式表演、迎神还愿或民间信仰叙事。": "The Five Directions General of the East from the Xiangdong Nuo mask series, Pingxiang. This is a character mask associated with Nuo drama or ritual in Xiangdong, Pingxiang, Jiangxi, used in ritual performance, welcoming deities, fulfilling vows or narratives of popular belief.",
  "萍乡湘东傩面具系列中的五方将（中）。该面具为江西萍乡湘东傩戏或傩仪中的角色面具，主要用于仪式表演、迎神还愿或民间信仰叙事。": "The Five Directions General of the Center from the Xiangdong Nuo mask series, Pingxiang. This is a character mask associated with Nuo drama or ritual in Xiangdong, Pingxiang, Jiangxi, used in ritual performance, welcoming deities, fulfilling vows or narratives of popular belief.",
  "萍乡湘东傩面具系列中的监查。该面具为江西萍乡湘东傩戏或傩仪中的角色面具，主要用于仪式表演、迎神还愿或民间信仰叙事。": "The Inspector from the Xiangdong Nuo mask series, Pingxiang. This is a character mask associated with Nuo drama or ritual in Xiangdong, Pingxiang, Jiangxi, used in ritual performance, welcoming deities, fulfilling vows or narratives of popular belief.",
  "萍乡湘东傩面具系列中的关老爷 ， 关帝君俗称关帝爷、关公、关老爷。关帝君的名是羽，字云长，本字长生，是三国蜀汉的大将。": "Lord Guan from the Xiangdong Nuo mask series, Pingxiang. Also called Guandi, Guan Gong or Guan Laoye, he is Guan Yu, courtesy name Yunchang and originally Changsheng, a major general of Shu Han during the Three Kingdoms period.",
  "萍乡湘东傩面具系列中的炎将军。该面具表现历史、小说或民间戏曲中的武将人物，通常用于突出忠勇、威严或护卫性的角色身份。": "General Yan from the Xiangdong Nuo mask series, Pingxiang. The mask portrays a military figure from history, fiction or folk drama, emphasizing loyalty, courage, authority or a protective role.",
  "石雕魌头”。此乃出土于比邻湘东区、经专家认定的西周文物。": "A stone-carved qitou head, excavated near Xiangdong District and identified by specialists as a Western Zhou artifact.",
  "花关索也称“关索”，据传为三国蜀将关羽之子。其参军后战功赫赫，最终成为精忠大义、神勇护国的大将，在婺源傩舞中作为重要的角色出现。花关索妻子为鲍家庄鲍王之女鲍三娘。": "Hua Guansuo, also known as Guan Suo, is said to be a son of the Shu general Guan Yu. After joining the army, he achieved great military success and became a loyal, righteous and courageous defender of the realm. He is an important character in Wuyuan Nuo dance. His wife, Bao Sanniang, is the daughter of King Bao of Bao Family Village.",
  "鲍三娘为江西傩舞角色花关索的妻子。角色在傩戏中有专门表现其姻缘的唱段。说唱词中提到，鲍三娘为鲍家庄鲍王之女，该女子巾帼不让须眉，许诺有能够战胜她者，愿嫁为妻，花关索遂与其比武，并战胜鲍三娘。鲍三娘于是履行诺言，与花关索结为夫妻，同下西川，立下赫赫战功。": "Bao Sanniang is the wife of Hua Guansuo, a character in Jiangxi Nuo dance. Dedicated sung passages tell the story of their marriage. The daughter of King Bao of Bao Family Village, she is a formidable fighter who promises to marry anyone who can defeat her. Hua Guansuo wins their contest, and she keeps her promise. They marry, campaign together in western Sichuan and achieve great military success.",
  "八十大王是江西婺源傩舞神灵系统中的主神之一，有研究婺源傩舞的专家认为，八十大王原型为黄帝时代的蚩尤。更有说法其前身为秦始皇长子扶苏太子，被其弟以毒酒暗害，死后成为傩神，专为人间斩妖驱鬼，扶正祛邪。": "Bashi Dawang, the Eightieth Great King, is one of the principal deities in Wuyuan Nuo dance, Jiangxi. Some researchers identify his prototype as Chiyou from the age of the Yellow Emperor. Another tradition identifies him as Prince Fusu, the eldest son of the First Emperor of Qin, murdered with poisoned wine by his younger brother. After death he becomes a Nuo deity who destroys demons, expels ghosts and upholds righteousness.",
  "吞口是我国民间使用的一种动物化的辟邪器物，与符箓、门神、灵兽、牙角、桃木、泰山石敢当一样，是民间辟邪的直观载体。吞口的称谓较多，江西称为“哨山”，台湾称“兽牌”，陕西称“辟邪”，在西南地区云、贵、川一带，普遍称“吞口”，此外，还有“天口”、“喷口”、“老虎牌等别称。吞口往往安放于宅门首、畜圈旁、寨门口，其目的是以辟邪消灾，保人畜平安。吞口在造型上，大致有两种形式，一种即是直接借用傩戏或傩舞中的某个面具的造型形象，如开山、开路先锋等，这类开山多为木雕。还有一种多为虎头造型形象，手工绘制于瓢勺形背面或葫芦上。": "Tunkou is an animal-like object used in popular religion to ward off evil, alongside talismans, door gods, protective beasts, teeth and horns, peachwood and Taishan Shigandang stones. It has many names: Shaoshan in Jiangxi, Shoupai in Taiwan and Bixie in Shaanxi. Tunkou is common in Yunnan, Guizhou and Sichuan; other names include Tiankou, Penkou and Tiger Plaque. Placed above house entrances, beside livestock pens or at village gates, it is intended to protect people and animals. Two broad forms occur: wooden carvings based on Nuo drama or dance masks, such as Kaishan or the Road-Opening Vanguard; and tiger heads painted on the back of a ladle or on a gourd.",
  "周将军 江西傩舞面具 ” 周将军是傩戏《唱三元》主神三元真君中的“下元定志周真君”，其原名为周斌，字文刚，与上元唐将军、中元葛将军为同父异母的兄弟。": "General Zhou, a Jiangxi Nuo dance mask. He is Zhou Zhenjun of the Lower Origin, one of the Three Primordial Lords who preside over the Nuo drama Singing the Three Origins. Originally named Zhou Bin, courtesy name Wengang, he shares a father with General Tang of the Upper Origin and General Ge of the Middle Origin.",
  "欧阳金甲大将军 江西傩舞面具 ” 欧阳金甲大将军是江西万载特有的傩神，又称大将军、大老爷，相传为二十四位冤死的乐师所化傩神之首。这二十四位乐师因为宋朝皇帝为试龙虎山张天师法力而受命藏于地窖装神弄鬼，却被张天师法术拆穿最终冤死阴魂不散，皇帝为安抚他们便将他们封作傩神。": "General Ouyang in Golden Armor, a Jiangxi Nuo dance mask. Unique to Wanzai, Jiangxi, he is also called the Great General or Great Lord. Legend makes him the leader of twenty-four Nuo deities formed from wrongfully killed musicians. A Song emperor ordered the musicians to hide in a cellar and impersonate spirits to test the powers of Celestial Master Zhang of Mount Longhu. Zhang's magic exposed them and they died unjustly. Their spirits would not rest, so the emperor conferred deity status on them.",
  "江西新干大洋洲出土的商代青铜傩面。该面具为江西傩戏或傩仪中的角色面具，主要用于仪式表演、迎神还愿或民间信仰叙事。": "A Shang-period bronze Nuo face excavated at Dayangzhou, Xingan, Jiangxi. The entry also describes it as a character mask associated with Jiangxi Nuo drama or ritual, used in ritual performance, welcoming deities, fulfilling vows or narratives of popular belief.",
  "江西傩文化源远流长，底蕴深厚，有着鲜明的地域风俗特色和独特的艺术价值，万载开口傩就是其中的优秀代表，为进一步培育和践行社会主义核心价值观，弘扬中华民族优秀传统文化。": "Jiangxi has a long and richly developed Nuo tradition, with distinctive local customs and artistic value. Wanzai's spoken Nuo drama is one representative form. The source presents its promotion as a way to support socialist core values and carry forward traditional Chinese culture.",
  "辰河戏面具鬼差， 辰河戏是一种传统戏曲剧种。主要流行于湖南沅水上、中游（旧属辰州） 辰河戏一带，以及与其毗邻的贵州、四川省部分地区。起源于明代迁徙到辰河的江西省移民。": "Ghost Attendant mask from Chenhe opera. This traditional opera form is found mainly in the upper and middle Yuan River area of Hunan, formerly Chenzhou, and neighboring parts of Guizhou and Sichuan. It originated among migrants from Jiangxi who settled in the Chenhe area during the Ming dynasty.",
  "周下元 唐上元、葛中元、周下元在全国不同地域的民间傩中常有出现，如江西婺源傩舞，可见相关神话传说在中华大地各民族间一直有着共同的传承，见证着文化的交往交流交融。三人分别为上元真君、中元真君、下元真君，合称三元真君。在不同种类的傩戏中司职也有所不同。": "Zhou Xiayuan. Tang of the Upper Origin, Ge of the Middle Origin and Zhou of the Lower Origin appear in Nuo traditions in different regions, including Wuyuan, Jiangxi. Their shared legends reflect cultural transmission and exchange among communities. Together they are the Three Primordial Lords; their particular duties vary between forms of Nuo drama.",
  "阴公傩面 阴公出现在傩戏剧目《降阴公》中，身份并不是某位固定的人物。在当地乡民心目中，阴公是他们信奉的神灵，若遇到什么病痛灾祸，便会请傩师表演傩戏以祭祀阴公祈求庇佑。": "Yin Gong mask. Yin Gong appears in the Nuo drama Invoking Yin Gong and does not identify one fixed historical person. Local villagers regard him as a deity. When illness or misfortune occurs, they may invite a Nuo specialist to perform drama in his honor and seek protection.",
  "清代傩戏面具“牛头”，牛头傩戏面具是重庆中国三峡博物馆收藏的乐器、法器类作品。面具特征:77938 文物类型:乐器、法器 实际数量:2 质量范围:0.01-1 kg 文物级别:一般 文物。": "Qing-period Ox Head Nuo mask, held by the Chongqing China Three Gorges Museum in the musical instruments and ritual implements category. The entry gives number 77938, quantity 2, weight range 0.01–1 kg, and classification as an ordinary cultural relic.",
  "该面具带有兽形、驱邪或原始祭仪意味，常通过夸张的口鼻、眼部和轮廓表现威慑力。": "This mask evokes animal forms, exorcism or early ritual practice. Exaggerated mouths, noses, eyes and outlines create an intimidating presence.",
  "该面具为重庆傩戏或傩仪中的角色面具，主要用于仪式表演、迎神还愿或民间信仰叙事。": "This is a character mask associated with Nuo drama or ritual in Chongqing, used in ritual performance, welcoming deities, fulfilling vows or narratives of popular belief.",
  "该面具表现佛教人物或僧侣形象，常用于呈现慈和、诙谐或劝善意味的角色。": "This mask portrays a Buddhist figure or monk, often conveying kindness, humor or encouragement to act well.",
  "乡约指在乡里中订立的共同遵守的规约；指奉官命在乡里中管事的人。保长是旧社会保甲制度的一个管理者，是以“户”（家庭）为社会组织的基本单位 保长相当于今天的社长，村长之类。参数。": "Xiangyue refers both to communal rules agreed within a locality and to a person appointed to manage local affairs. A baozhang was an administrator in the former baojia system, organized around households, roughly comparable to a community or village head. The source ends with a generic parameters label.",
  "勾愿刹官 参数。该面具多属驱邪、引路、判察或仪式护法角色，在傩戏中承担开场、镇邪或沟通神鬼的功能。": "Gouyuan Shaguan. The source includes a parameters label. This mask is associated with exorcism, guiding, judgment or ritual protection, serving to open performances, subdue evil or communicate with deities and spirits in Nuo drama.",
  "牛皋[gāo]（1087年～1147年），汝州鲁山（今河南省鲁山县）人，南宋抗金名将、民族英雄。牛皋出身农民家庭，初为射士，精练武功，擅长骑射。南宋初年聚集人民抗金。绍兴三年（1133年），加入岳家军、长胜军。牛皋使用双锏，乃金所制。后隶归岳飞，为其推重，对金作战中屡立战功。曾参加镇压杨幺起义。岳飞被害后，因始终反对宋金议和，被秦桧害死。参数。": "Niu Gao (1087–1147), from Lushan in Ruzhou, now Lushan County, Henan, was a Southern Song general noted for resisting the Jin. Born into a farming family, he trained in martial arts and mounted archery and first served as an archer. He gathered people to resist the Jin in the early Southern Song and joined Yue Fei's forces and the Ever-Victorious Army in 1133. He wielded paired metal jian batons and earned Yue Fei's esteem through repeated military successes. He also helped suppress Yang Yao's rebellion. After Yue Fei was killed, Niu Gao continued to oppose peace with the Jin and was killed through Qin Hui's actions. The source ends with a generic parameters label.",
  "该面具对应民间信仰中的神祇角色，多与护佑地方、祈福禳灾、风雨收成或仪式迎神有关。": "This mask represents a deity in popular religion, associated with protecting a locality, seeking blessings, averting misfortune, rain and harvests, or welcoming deities in ritual.",
  "该面具多属驱邪、引路、判察或仪式护法角色，在傩戏中承担开场、镇邪或沟通神鬼的功能。": "This mask is associated with exorcism, guiding, judgment or ritual protection, serving to open performances, subdue evil or communicate with deities and spirits in Nuo drama.",
  "艺术价值：如今傩戏已被更多人所熟知，而二郎神面具的雕刻艺术正日渐成为引人瞩目的民间工艺品，并凸显出其独特的收藏价值。": "Artistic value: as Nuo drama becomes more widely known, the carving of Erlang Shen masks has attracted attention as a folk craft and for its distinctive value to collectors.",
  "蜀主刘备，称帝成都，国号蜀汉，使四川成为与吴魏鼎立的强国，在短时间内繁荣昌盛，四川民众引以为荣地供奉他为蜀地之主，称成都为“天子之都”，在这里也把他塑造成为和善亲切的邻家老大爷。刘备（161年-223年6月10日），字玄德，东汉末年幽州涿郡涿县（今河北省涿州市）人，西汉中山靖王刘胜之后，三国时期蜀汉开国皇帝，年号章武。": "Liu Bei, Lord of Shu, became emperor in Chengdu and named his state Shu Han. Sichuan thus became one of the three powers alongside Wu and Wei and experienced a period of prosperity. Local people honored him as the Lord of Shu and called Chengdu the emperor's capital. Here he is portrayed as a kindly, approachable elderly neighbor. Liu Bei (161–10 June 223), courtesy name Xuande, came from Zhuo County in Zhuo Commandery, now Zhuozhou, Hebei. A descendant of Liu Sheng, Prince Jing of Zhongshan, he founded Shu Han during the Three Kingdoms period and used the reign title Zhangwu.",
  "土主张飞，因在蜀国期间镇守阆中，使得西蜀一方水土安宁、人民安居乐业，所以四川人供奉其为神。": "Zhang Fei, the Local Lord. While serving Shu, he defended Langzhong, bringing security and stability to the area. People in Sichuan therefore worshiped him as a deity.",
  "川主二郎神，相传为李冰次子李二郎，二郎真君的道观在四川灌江口（今成都都江堰），西游记中这样描述二郎神：“仪容清俊貌堂堂，两耳垂肩目有光。头戴三山飞凤帽，身穿一领淡鹅黄。缕金靴衬盘龙袜，玉带团花八宝妆。腰挎弹弓新月样，手执三尖两刃枪。斧劈桃山曾救母，弹打棕罗双凤凰。力诛八怪声名远，义结梅山七圣行。心高不识天家眷，性傲归神住灌江。赤诚昭惠英灵圣，显化无边号二郎。”很显然，二郎神在西游记里面是一个玉树临风的大帅哥。": "Erlang Shen, Lord of Sichuan, is said to be Li Erlang, the second son of Li Bing. His temple is at Guanjiangkou, now Dujiangyan, Chengdu. Journey to the West describes a handsome, dignified figure with long ears and shining eyes, wearing a phoenix crown and pale yellow robe, gold-decorated boots and a jeweled jade belt. He carries a crescent-shaped slingshot and a three-pointed, double-edged spear. The verse recalls his rescue of his mother from Mount Tao, his feats against birds and monsters, and his fellowship with the Seven Sages of Meishan. Proud and independent, he returns to Guanjiang rather than defer to the heavenly court. The passage presents Erlang as a strikingly handsome figure.",
  "报虎，面具作为傩戏的道具，需要根据戏中角色雕刻运用，《出报虎》是傩戏中的一出插戏，舞者戴上面具，扭动下肢，达到镇妖降魔的效果。“戏如人生，人生如戏”，傩戏中的千姿百态就是芸芸众生的缩影。或哭、或笑、或嘻、或怒、或骂、或癫......都凝聚在这一瞬间。": "Bao Hu. Nuo masks are carved and used according to theatrical roles. The interlude Bringing Out Bao Hu features a masked dancer twisting the lower body to subdue demons. The source compares the varied crying, laughter, playfulness, anger, scolding and frenzy of Nuo drama to the many expressions of human life, captured in a single moment.",
  "账房先生，根据世俗形象塑造，发辫盘起，戴着眼镜，一副幽默精明的样子。": "The Accountant is modeled on a worldly character: his braid is coiled up, he wears glasses, and his expression is humorous and shrewd.",
  "回回，即回纥，回鹘。回纥是维吾尔族及裕固族等族的宗源。在七世纪初，回纥和吐蕃在北方和西方立国，对中国历史有深远的影响。在四川，回回人的定居历史悠久，但因为回回是少数民族，在傩戏中往往被贬化为头戴瓜皮帽，画着花脸的小丑角色，逗乐观众。": "Huihui. The entry associates this term with the historical Huihe or Huigu peoples, among the ancestors of the Uyghurs and Yugurs, and discusses the influence of northern and western states in early Chinese history. It notes a long history of Huihui settlement in Sichuan. In Nuo drama, however, this minority character was often reduced to a comic stereotype, wearing a small rounded cap and painted face to amuse the audience.",
  "娃儿，根据世俗形象创作，一般头上有髻，俏皮可爱。": "The Child is modeled on an everyday figure, usually with a topknot and a lively, endearing expression.",
  "电母，与雷公一起担负着行云布雨的职责，在傩戏中用于求雨仪式。": "Dianmu, the Lightning Mother, shares responsibility with Leigong for clouds and rain and appears in Nuo rain-seeking rituals.",
  "龙王，作为水神，掌管着雨水的施取。对于靠天吃饭的农耕社会尤为重要。在傩戏中用来求雨或是祈盼来年风调雨顺以及还愿。": "The Dragon King governs rainfall as a water deity and is particularly important in farming societies dependent on the weather. Nuo performances invoke him to request rain, seek favorable weather for the coming year or fulfill vows.",
  "春官，本为古官名，颛顼氏时的五官之一，春官以大宗伯为长官，掌理礼制、祭祀、历法等事。在傩戏中，春官的主要职责是恭贺新禧、推销历书。": "Chunguan, the Spring Official, was originally an ancient official title, described as one of the five offices under Zhuanxu. Headed by the Grand Master of Ceremonies, it oversaw rites, sacrifices and the calendar. In Nuo drama, the Spring Official mainly offers New Year greetings and sells almanacs.",
  "在傩戏中消灾和尚常自诩为替罪替难身“，把人们认为不吉利的东西全都收归于自己，一副我不入地狱，谁入地狱“的慈悲模样，备受人们喜欢。": "The Disaster-Dispelling Monk in Nuo drama describes himself as a substitute who accepts others' guilt and misfortune, taking all things thought inauspicious upon himself. His compassionate willingness to suffer for others makes him a well-liked character.",
  "消灾和尚，又称减灾和尚“，一般以挤眉弄眼、豁牙露齿的形象出现，能帮人消灾去难、逢凶化吉。": "The Disaster-Dispelling Monk, also called the Disaster-Reducing Monk, usually appears winking and grimacing with missing or exposed teeth. He is believed to help avert calamity and turn misfortune into good fortune.",
  "蚕丝公，是四川面具中独有的。因蜀地盛产桑而多有蚕虫，蜀锦久负盛名、盛极一时，三国时期，蜀锦曾是蜀国军备开支的重要。": "Cansi Gong, the Silkworm Lord, is described as unique to Sichuan masks. Mulberry cultivation and silkworm raising flourished in Shu, whose brocade became famous. The entry links Shu brocade to military expenditure during the Three Kingdoms period, but the final sentence is incomplete.",
  "小鬼，一般作为钟馗的随从，协助捉拿妖魔鬼怪。": "The Little Ghost generally serves as an attendant to Zhong Kui, helping capture demons and ghosts.",
  "钟馗，”钟馗捉鬼“最为人知晓，人们认为他法力无边、有求必应，把他看作是诸神中的万应之神，广为供奉。": "Zhong Kui is best known for catching ghosts. Believers regard his powers as limitless and responsive to appeals, and worship him widely as a deity who answers many kinds of prayers.",
  "傩公傩母，在傩仪的神坛上供奉的最为普遍，他们是傩俗信仰中至高无上、最具威望的傩，开坛仪式前都要请出来祭拜。": "Nuo Gong and Nuo Mu are commonly honored on Nuo ritual altars. They are regarded as supreme and highly authoritative deities in Nuo belief and are brought out for worship before the altar-opening rite.",
  "武财神，民间一般称赵公明为武财神。《三教搜神大全》称其能驱雷役电，唤雨呼风，除瘟剪疟，保病禳灾“。": "The Martial God of Wealth is commonly identified as Zhao Gongming. The Compendium of the Search for Deities of the Three Teachings credits him with commanding thunder and lightning, summoning wind and rain, removing epidemics and malaria, and protecting people from illness and misfortune.",
  "四川民间对二郎神的崇拜最为兴盛，凡驱瘟逐疫、降妖镇宅、整治水患、节令赛会灯各种民俗行为，莫不搬请二郎神。": "Worship of Erlang Shen is particularly prominent in Sichuan. He is invoked in folk practices involving epidemics, demons, household protection, flood control and seasonal celebrations.",
  "土主张飞，因在蜀国期间镇守阆中，使得西蜀一方水土安宁、人民安居乐业，所以四川人供奉其为神。张飞，字翼德，是中国历史上著名的三国时期蜀汉名将，与刘备、关羽并称为“桃园三结义”。他勇猛善战，忠诚耿直，是中国历史上一位杰出的军事统帅。": "Zhang Fei, the Local Lord. During Shu rule he defended Langzhong and brought security to the surrounding region, leading people in Sichuan to worship him as a deity. Courtesy name Yide, Zhang Fei was a celebrated general of Shu Han in the Three Kingdoms period. With Liu Bei and Guan Yu, he forms the trio of the Peach Garden Oath. He is remembered as a brave, loyal and forthright military commander.",
  "川主是流行于中国巴蜀地区以及其它巴蜀移民聚居地的重要民间信仰，起源于唐朝及之前四川地区对于秦蜀郡太守李冰及二郎神的信仰崇拜，是一种以巴蜀治水文化为核心内容的民间信仰，求川主以保佑巴蜀免于水旱灾害。": "Worship of Chuanzhu, Lord of Sichuan, is important in the Bashu region and communities of Bashu migrants. It developed from the worship of Li Bing, Qin governor of Shu, and Erlang Shen in Sichuan during or before the Tang dynasty. Centered on the region's water-management traditions, it seeks protection against floods and droughts.",
  "祭龙节主要流行于云南等地的彝族聚居区。这个节日通常选在每年清明前后的半个月内，特别是在属龙的日子进行。例如，在四川省会理县小黑箐乡白沙村，村民们会在大黑山的龙洞水口举行祭龙仪式。而云南的彝族地区，尤其是红河县宝华乡座落村的彝族，也普遍存有崇龙习俗，他们认为“龙不仅仅是雨水的象征，还是集多种神灵于一身的村寨保护神。二郎神又号灌口二郎，起源于四川灌县（今四川都江堰市）由治水英雄崇拜而衍化的泛水神信仰。郎神俊雅衣黄，力大无穷，法术无边，通晓八九玄功，阙庭有神眼，手持三尖两刃刀。宋朝将二郎神纳入朝廷祀典，并诏修神保观专作供奉。": "The Dragon Worship Festival is found in Yi communities in Yunnan and elsewhere, usually within about two weeks of Qingming, especially on a dragon day. In Baisha Village, Xiaoheiqing Township, Huili, Sichuan, rituals take place at the outlet of the Dragon Cave on Dahei Mountain. Yi communities such as Zuoluo Village in Baohua Township, Honghe County, Yunnan, regard the dragon not only as a symbol of rain but as a village protector embodying several divine powers. The entry then describes Erlang Shen, also called Guankou Erlang, whose worship developed from reverence for water-control heroes in Guan County, now Dujiangyan. He is portrayed as handsome, dressed in yellow, immensely strong and magically skilled, with a divine eye on his forehead and a three-pointed, double-edged weapon. The Song court incorporated him into official worship and ordered the construction of Shenbao Temple.",
  "豹头面具， 祭龙节主要流行于云南等地的彝族聚居区。这个节日通常选在每年清明前后的半个月内，特别是在属龙的日子进行。例如，在四川省会理县小黑箐乡白沙村，村民们会在大黑山的龙洞水口举行祭龙仪式。而云南的彝族地区，尤其是红河县宝华乡座落村的彝族，也普遍存有崇龙习俗，他们认为“龙不仅仅是雨水的象征，还是集多种神灵于一身的村寨保护神。": "Leopard Head mask. The Dragon Worship Festival is found in Yi communities in Yunnan and elsewhere, usually within about two weeks of Qingming, especially on a dragon day. In Baisha Village, Xiaoheiqing Township, Huili, Sichuan, rituals take place at the outlet of the Dragon Cave on Dahei Mountain. Yi communities such as Zuoluo Village in Baohua Township, Honghe County, Yunnan, regard the dragon not only as a symbol of rain but as a village protector embodying several divine powers.",
  "双峰傩戏面具大全，感受独特的傩文化的魅力。四川双峰傩面具又称为“脸壳子”，起初是用蔑条挽成各个人物脸庞大小的蔑圈，傩戏艺人根据不同脸庞用报纸粘糊成形，再根据纸糊成形的脸壳，用画笔圈圈点点的描绘上五颜六色。": "A collection of Shuangfeng Nuo drama masks introduces the distinctive local tradition. In Sichuan, these masks are also called liankezhi, or face shells. Makers initially bent bamboo strips into face-sized frames, pasted newspaper over them to form a shell, then painted the faces in many colors.",
  "倮倮，就是彝族，彝族人崇拜老虎和龙，老虎在彝族语中说的就是luo，龙是lu,他们用自己崇拜的东西来命名自己的种族，认为自己是龙和虎的后代。由于旧时民族间缺乏交流，一般外族人称彝族为倮倮，则带有某些侮辱性，在傩戏中将其塑造为歪鼻斜眼、龇牙咧嘴的形象。": "Luoluo is a historical name for the Yi. The entry links Yi identity to reverence for tigers and dragons and to words rendered as luo and lu, describing the people as descendants of these animals. It also notes that outsiders' use of Luoluo carried derogatory implications. Nuo drama reflects that prejudice in a distorted, mocking figure with a crooked nose, slanted eyes and bared teeth.",
  "俗称“吞口的镇宅面具，不是用来戴在脸上，而是常悬挂在门楣上，既有木雕漆绘也有葫芦瓢绘。常见于彝族、水族、汉族等民族之中。云南民族民间所见的吞口造型多为虎头，常常有长柄，保持勺柄状，便于悬挂。用葫芦瓢做成的吞口，多在淡黄的底色上勾勒出五官，再施彩绘。木雕吞口口含短剑，两眼突凸，龇牙咧嘴，凶神恶煞。水族的漆绘木雕吞口，还具有脸谱画法的装饰韵味。": "Tunkou household-protection masks are normally hung above doorways rather than worn. They may be painted wooden carvings or painted gourd ladles, and occur among Yi, Shui, Han and other communities. In Yunnan, many take the form of tiger heads with long, ladle-like handles for hanging. Gourd examples often have features outlined and colored over a pale yellow ground. Wooden examples may hold a short sword in the mouth, with bulging eyes, bared teeth and a fierce expression. Painted wooden Shui examples also have decorative qualities resembling theatrical face painting.",
  "俗称“吞口的镇宅面具，不是用来戴在脸上，而是常悬挂在门楣上，既有木雕漆绘也有葫芦瓢绘。云南民族民间所见的吞口造型多为虎头，常常有长柄，保持勺柄状，便于悬挂。用葫芦瓢做成的吞口，多在淡黄的底色上勾勒出五官，再施彩绘。木雕吞口口含短剑，两眼突凸，龇牙咧嘴，凶神恶煞。水族的漆绘木雕吞口，还具有脸谱画法的装饰韵味。": "Tunkou household-protection masks are normally hung above doorways rather than worn. They may be painted wooden carvings or painted gourd ladles. In Yunnan, many take the form of tiger heads with long, ladle-like handles for hanging. Gourd examples often have features outlined and colored over a pale yellow ground. Wooden examples may hold a short sword in the mouth, with bulging eyes, bared teeth and a fierce expression. Painted wooden Shui examples also have decorative qualities resembling theatrical face painting.",
  "白族笑和尚面具是中国云南省白族民间传统的一种面具艺术形式。这种面具以其独特的风格和深厚的文化内涵而著称，在白族的民间信仰和节庆活动中占有重要的地位。": "The Bai Laughing Monk mask is a traditional form of mask art among the Bai people of Yunnan. Known for its distinctive style and cultural associations, it has an important place in Bai popular belief and festive activities.",
  "堆沙节,傣语称“广母赛”,是德宏傣族、德昂族等民族的传统节日,主要是为了庆祝丰收,祈求来年风调雨顺,通常是在傣历一月十五日,也就是傣族“出洼后的一个月举行。": "The Sand-Piling Festival, called Guangmusai in Dai, is a traditional festival of the Dai, De'ang and other peoples in Dehong. It celebrates the harvest and seeks favorable weather for the next year. The entry places it on the fifteenth day of the first Dai month, about a month after the end of the Buddhist rains retreat.",
  "傣族孔雀舞，云南省瑞丽市民间传统舞蹈，国家非物质文化遗产之一。傣族孔雀舞流布于云南省德宏傣族景颇族自治州的瑞丽、潞西及西双版纳、孟定、孟达、景谷、沧源等傣族聚居区。该面具为云南傩戏或傩仪中的角色面具，主要用于仪式表演、迎神还愿或民间信仰叙事。": "The Dai Peacock Dance, associated here with Ruili, Yunnan, is a traditional folk dance listed as national intangible cultural heritage. It is practiced in Dai communities in Ruili and Luxi in Dehong, and in Xishuangbanna, Mengding, Mengda, Jinggu and Cangyuan. The entry also describes the mask as a character mask used in Yunnan Nuo drama or ritual for performances, welcoming deities, fulfilling vows or narratives of popular belief.",
  "关索戏属于傩戏剧种，初为古代用以驱邪逐疫的傩祭舞蹈、仪式，北宋时传入宫廷后，才逐渐从傩舞向表达故事情节的小戏形式发展，逐渐发展成娱神娱人兼有的古老而独特的戏剧。其面具一般为浓眉、大眼、虎口、勾鼻，威武勇猛，意在降妖伏魔。": "Guansuo opera is a form of Nuo drama. The entry traces it to exorcistic dances and rituals intended to repel disease, and describes a gradual development into short narrative plays after entering the court in the Northern Song. It came to combine entertainment for deities and people. Its masks commonly feature thick brows, large eyes, tiger-like mouths and hooked noses, creating a powerful appearance intended to subdue demons.",
  "汉族傩戏猴子面具，观看。该面具带有兽形、驱邪或原始祭仪意味，常通过夸张的口鼻、眼部和轮廓表现威慑力。": "A Monkey mask from Han Nuo drama. This mask evokes animal forms, exorcism or early ritual practice. Exaggerated mouths, noses, eyes and outlines create an intimidating presence.",
  "寿星又称南极老人星，星名，古代神话中的的长寿之神。也是道教中的神仙，本为恒星名，为福、禄、寿三星之一。民间认为供奉这位仙神，可以使人健康长寿，这位仙神其实是道教追求长生的一种信仰。": "Shouxing, also known as the Old Man of the South Pole, is a longevity deity in traditional mythology and Daoism. Originally a star name, he is one of the three stellar deities of Blessing, Prosperity and Longevity. Worshipers seek health and long life through him, expressing the Daoist aspiration to longevity.",
  "魁星是中国神话传说中的一位神仙，原称奎星，又称“天豕”、“封豕”，为二十八星宿之一，主宰天下文运，在儒士学子心目中，具有至高无上的地位，是读书士子的守护神。其形貌黑脸红发以鬼面出现，右手执朱批笔、左手托金印，左脚后翘踢斗，因此也被称为魁又名文魁夫子、大魁夫子、大魁星君、绿衣帝君、魁星爷等。": "Kuixing is a deity in Chinese mythology, originally associated with the Kui star or constellation and also called Tianshi or Fengshi. Described here as one of the twenty-eight lunar lodges, he governs literary success and is revered as a protector of scholars. He appears with a black, ghost-like face and red hair, holding a red marking brush in his right hand and a gold seal in his left, with his left foot raised backward to kick the Dipper. Other titles include Wenkui Fuzi, Dakui Fuzi, Dakui Xingjun, the Green-Robed Emperor and Lord Kuixing.",
  "瑶族“度戎面具。该面具为云南傩戏或傩仪中的角色面具，主要用于仪式表演、迎神还愿或民间信仰叙事。": "A Yao Durong mask. The entry describes it as a character mask associated with Nuo drama or ritual in Yunnan, used in ritual performance, welcoming deities, fulfilling vows or narratives of popular belief.",
  "彝族大刀舞是漾濞有名的民族民间舞蹈,传统的大刀舞通常与打歌同场表演,男性舞刀者在场中央独舞,众打歌者在旁围成一圈和着笛子、芦笙及对歌声打跳。": "The Yi Broadsword Dance is a well-known folk dance of Yangbi. Traditionally it is performed alongside dage communal singing and dancing: a male sword dancer performs in the center while others form a circle, stepping and dancing to flutes, lusheng reed instruments and antiphonal singing.",
  "狮虎舞有求神娱神的本意，也有欢庆祝福的喜悦，彝族撒尼的狮虎舞在一些动作上与中国传统体育舞狮有很多相似之处，是撒尼民族文化的瑰宝，是撒尼民俗体育的具体体现。狮虎舞是盛传于昆明市石林彝族自治县撒尼山寨的传统舞蹈。“狮虎舞在撒尼人居住的村寨都必须有，因为送葬老人时，舅舅家、娘娘家必须组织狮虎舞队来参加送葬，历史渊源流长。后来此舞蹈走上了大众舞台，无论是红白喜事或重大节庆活动，都离不开“狮虎舞这一传统舞蹈。": "The Lion–Tiger Dance combines appeals to deities, entertainment for them and expressions of celebration and blessing. Some movements in the Sani Yi form resemble traditional Chinese lion dancing. Practiced in Sani villages in Shilin Yi Autonomous County, Kunming, it is an important expression of local culture and physical tradition. At elders' funerals, the maternal relatives' families traditionally organize Lion–Tiger Dance teams to join the procession. The dance later reached public stages and remains part of weddings, funerals and major festivals.",
  "刘邦手下的大将樊哙。在“统兵回山的法事中出场，检查阴兵所收魂魄是否已经交给失魂之人。该面具为武将造型，立眉竖眼，形象威猛。": "Fan Kuai, a general serving Liu Bang, appears in the rite Leading the Troops Back to the Mountain. He checks whether the souls recovered by spirit troops have been returned to those who lost them. The mask has a powerful warrior form with upright brows and staring eyes.",
  "据说是盘古的化身，在“山王取魂的法事中出场。阴兵不能取回的魂魄，便由山王前去追索，该面具为龙头造型。": "Said to be an incarnation of Pangu, the Mountain King appears in the rite The Mountain King Retrieves the Soul. He pursues souls that the spirit troops cannot recover. The mask takes the form of a dragon head.",
  "土地主管一方土地的小神，是慈祥幽默的老者形象。": "Tudi is a minor deity responsible for a local area of land, portrayed as a kindly and humorous old man.",
  "在“和尚检斋的法事中出场，主要查看主人家是否诚心、法事流程是否合乎规则。面具造型是秃头圆脸、大耳阔口，眉开眼笑，头上还有一个凸起的包，俗称“福包”。": "This character appears in the rite The Monk Inspects the Offering, checking the host family's sincerity and whether the ritual follows the rules. The mask has a bald, round head, large ears, a broad smiling mouth and a bump on the head commonly called the blessing bump.",
  "药王负责驱逐灾病的正神，头戴冠帽，眼睛突出。": "Yaowang, the Medicine King, is a benevolent deity responsible for driving away illness. He wears a crown or official hat and has protruding eyes.",
  "巫师公傩戏中的巫师，俗称“端公”，红面长髯，双耳垂肩。": "Wushigong is a ritual specialist in Nuo drama, commonly called Duangong. He has a red face, a long beard and ears that hang toward his shoulders.",
  "牧牛童子傩戏中的配角，童子形象。该面具带有兽形、驱邪或原始祭仪意味，常通过夸张的口鼻、眼部和轮廓表现威慑力。": "The Cowherd Boy is a childlike supporting character in Nuo drama. The entry also describes the mask in general terms as evoking animal forms, exorcism or early ritual, using exaggerated facial features and outlines to create an intimidating presence.",
  "小鬼是傩戏中的配角，鬼兵的形象，蓝面、尖头。": "The Little Ghost is a supporting character in Nuo drama, depicted as a spirit soldier with a blue face and pointed head.",
  "灵官即王灵官，是赫赫有名的道教护法神，掌天下人间的纠察之职，他在傩堂中的任务是搜捕混入傩堂的邪魔妖鬼。灵官面具，模样凶猛，面色赤红，头上戴着道冠，额际上有一只混赤眼，亦称“纵目”。": "Lingguan is Wang Lingguan, a prominent Daoist guardian responsible for inspecting the human world. In the Nuo hall he searches for evil spirits that have entered the ritual space. His mask is fierce and bright red, with a Daoist crown and an additional red eye on the forehead, also called a vertical eye.",
  "花脸男性。他身穿法衣，腰围战衩腰带，手持青龙剑一把，全身武将装饰。他在傩戏《关爷斩蔡琴》中与关公对战数回合，结果被关公用计谋斩杀。": "A male character with a painted face. He wears ritual robes and a warrior's sash, carries a Green Dragon sword and is dressed as a military figure. In the Nuo drama Lord Guan Slays Cai Qin, he fights several rounds against Guan Gong before being killed through Guan's strategy.",
  "黑脸男性。此人是关公的马夫。他身穿号褂战衩，手持宝剑。该角色在傩戏《关爷斩蔡琴》中有“三哭蔡阳之经典唱段。": "A black-faced male character who serves as Guan Gong's groom. He wears a military tunic and battle skirt and carries a sword. In the Nuo drama Lord Guan Slays Cai Qin, he performs the well-known passage Three Laments for Cai Yang.",
  "傩公，红脸男性。傩母，白脸女性，任何一坛傩戏都首先要在傩堂正中供奉傩公傩母，才能保佑这坛傩戏顺利进行，也才能达到主家的目的。": "Nuo Gong is a red-faced male figure and Nuo Mu a white-faced female figure. The description says that they must first be honored at the center of the Nuo hall so the performance can proceed successfully and fulfill the host family's purpose.",
  "傩母（右） 傩公，红脸男性。傩母，白脸女性，任何一坛傩戏都首先要在傩堂正中供奉傩公傩母，才能保佑这坛傩戏顺利进行，也才能达到主家的目的。": "Nuo Mu, at right. Nuo Gong is a red-faced male figure and Nuo Mu a white-faced female figure. The description says that they must first be honored at the center of the Nuo hall so the performance can proceed successfully and fulfill the host family's purpose.",
  "该面具为未明确地区傩戏或傩仪中的角色面具，主要用于仪式表演、迎神还愿或民间信仰叙事。": "This is a character mask associated with Nuo drama or ritual from an unspecified region, used in ritual performance, welcoming deities, fulfilling vows or narratives of popular belief.",
  "马面傩戏面具，马头傩戏面具。面具上的神态丰富多样，有的面具生动而夸张，有的则神秘而威严。在古代，不论官方民间，皆祭马神。周朝时，官方的祭祀制度是：春祭马祖，夏祭先牧，秋祭马社，冬祭马步。马祖是天驷星，先牧是最初教人牧马的神灵，马社是马厩中的土地神，马步是给马带来灾害的灾神。民间多有马王庙、马神庙。骡马驴商贩、马帮都将马王爷示为行业神。马是君主仁德，马是太平盛世。马是刚健，马是热烈，马是御雨乘风，马是不舍昼夜。": "Horse Face or Horse Head Nuo mask. Expressions range from vivid and exaggerated to mysterious and imposing. Both official and popular horse-deity worship existed in antiquity. The entry describes Zhou seasonal rites for Mazu in spring, Xianmu in summer, Mashe in autumn and Mabu in winter: respectively the Heavenly Quadriga star, the deity who first taught horse herding, the earth deity of the stable and a deity of equine calamity. Horse King and Horse God temples were widespread, and horse, mule and donkey traders and caravan drivers treated the Horse King as their patron. The source associates horses with benevolent rule, peaceful prosperity, strength, passion, movement through wind and rain, and tireless effort.",
  "傩公傩母面具有些地区传说傩公傩母其实也就是伏羲女娲，也就是洪水神话中再造人类的那对兄妹，土家族地区将其当作族人的始祖。": "Nuo Gong and Nuo Mu masks. In some regional traditions they are identified with Fuxi and Nüwa, the brother and sister who recreate humanity after a flood. Tujia communities regard them as ancestral figures.",
  "婺源傩舞戏面具造型介于写实与抽象之间，似人似神，自成风格。这件面具是婺源压轴鬼舞戏《舞花》中的角色——秦朝丞相李斯。这场戏表现的是秦始皇长子扶苏被奸贼用毒计害死的故事，出场人物有扶苏、蒙恬、李斯等。丞相李斯生于战国末年，是秦朝著名的政治家，协助秦始皇统一天下，参与制定法律，统一文字、度量衡等。秦始皇死后，李斯为了一己私利，听从赵高的诡计，害死了太子扶苏，成了秦二世的帮凶，后来被赵高所忌，以谋反罪名陷害至死。艺术价值：如今傩戏已被更多人所熟知，而傩面具的雕刻艺术正日渐成为引人瞩目的民间工艺品，并凸显出其独特的收藏价值。": "Wuyuan Nuo dance masks combine realism and abstraction, appearing both human and divine. This mask represents Li Si, the Qin chancellor, in the concluding ghost-dance drama Wuhua. The drama tells how Fusu, the First Emperor's eldest son, is killed through treachery, with Fusu, Meng Tian and Li Si among its characters. Li Si helped the First Emperor unify the realm and establish laws and standardized writing, weights and measures. After the emperor's death, he followed Zhao Gao's plot for personal advantage, contributed to Fusu's death and supported the Second Emperor. Zhao Gao later framed him for rebellion and had him killed. The entry adds that growing awareness of Nuo drama has drawn attention to mask carving as a folk craft and collectible art form.",
  "艺术价值：如今傩戏已被更多人所熟知，而七十二侯文官面具的雕刻艺术正日渐成为引人瞩目的民间工艺品，并凸显出其独特的收藏价值。": "Artistic value: as Nuo drama becomes more widely known, the carving of Seventy-Two Lords Civil Official masks has attracted attention as a folk craft and for its distinctive value to collectors.",
  "艺术价值：如今傩戏已被更多人所熟知，而东大神面具的雕刻艺术正日渐成为引人瞩目的民间工艺品，并凸显出其独特的收藏价值。": "Artistic value: as Nuo drama becomes more widely known, the carving of Great Eastern Deity masks has attracted attention as a folk craft and for its distinctive value to collectors.",
  "艺术价值：如今傩戏已被更多人所熟知，而白面东大神面具的雕刻艺术正日渐成为引人瞩目的民间工艺品，并凸显出其独特的收藏价值。": "Artistic value: as Nuo drama becomes more widely known, the carving of White-Faced Great Eastern Deity masks has attracted attention as a folk craft and for its distinctive value to collectors.",
  "开路先锋是专为奔赴傩坛的各路神祗打开东西南北方通道的开路神。暴眼圆睁，獠牙锋利、凶恶威武。": "The Road-Opening Vanguard opens paths in all four directions for the deities traveling to the Nuo altar. Wide, bulging eyes and sharp fangs give him a fierce, imposing appearance.",
  "土地为主管一方的乡神，名目甚多，有九个弟兄，专为主家纳祥驱邪赐福添寿。土地面具造型稳重，神态安祥，慈眉善目，两耳肥大，统为男性。此面具原本有胡须，因使用年代久远，胡须已完全脱落。": "Tudi is a local land deity with many titles. The description speaks of nine brothers who bring auspiciousness, drive away evil and bestow blessings and longevity on the host family. Tudi masks are male, composed and peaceful, with kindly features and large ears. This mask originally had a beard, but prolonged use has caused it to fall away completely.",
  "吞口是云、贵、川、湘等省一些少数民族地区挂在门楣上，用于驱邪的木雕。怪兽绘太极八卦图，豹眼怒视，龇牙咧嘴，犬齿突出，血口洞开，好似能吞掉一切灾祸和妖魔鬼怪，保佑风调雨顺，避邪救灾免疫。": "Tunkou are wooden carvings hung above doorways to ward off evil in some minority communities in Yunnan, Guizhou, Sichuan and Hunan. The monstrous face is decorated with a taiji and bagua design, glaring leopard-like eyes, exposed teeth, protruding fangs and a gaping red mouth. It appears able to swallow disasters and evil spirits, protecting favorable weather and averting calamity and disease.",
  "王灵官，天宫里的纠察神。清代遗存的傩面具，彩绘，马尾装饰，出自昭通镇雄县。王灵官是一位额有神眼，与神火密不可分的神灵，故而在傩坛中，常将王灵官作为送神逐疫的神灵，借其神火驱除鬼魅、消灭不洁不祥。": "Wang Lingguan, the inspecting deity of the heavenly palace. This painted Qing-period Nuo mask, decorated with horsehair, comes from Zhenxiong County, Zhaotong. Wang Lingguan has a divine eye on his forehead and is closely associated with sacred fire. At Nuo altars he is invoked to send off deities and expel disease, using his fire to remove ghosts and impurity.",
  "八蛮将军。民国时期遗存的傩面具，彩绘，出自昭通镇雄县。": "Baman General. A painted Nuo mask surviving from the Republican period, from Zhenxiong County, Zhaotong.",
  "丑娘彩，表现妇女分娩瞬间喜悦与痛苦交织的瞬间情态。清代遗存的傩面具，出自昭通镇雄县。": "Chou Niangcai portrays the intermingled joy and pain of a woman giving birth. This Qing-period Nuo mask comes from Zhenxiong County, Zhaotong.",
  "李二郎，即秦国时期蜀郡太守李冰，主持修筑都江堰。树皮制，建国后遗存的傩面具，出自昭通大关县。": "Li Erlang. The source identifies this figure with Li Bing, Qin governor of Shu and leader of the Dujiangyan irrigation project. A bark Nuo mask dating after 1949, from Daguan County, Zhaotong.",
  "唐叔贵池傩戏”。该面具为未明确地区傩戏或傩仪中的角色面具，主要用于仪式表演、迎神还愿或民间信仰叙事。": "Tang Shu, labeled Guichi Nuo drama. The entry also categorizes it as a character mask from an unspecified region, used in ritual performance, welcoming deities, fulfilling vows or narratives of popular belief.",
  "虎面贵池傩戏”。该面具带有兽形、驱邪或原始祭仪意味，常通过夸张的口鼻、眼部和轮廓表现威慑力。": "Tiger Face, labeled Guichi Nuo drama. This mask evokes animal forms, exorcism or early ritual practice. Exaggerated mouths, noses, eyes and outlines create an intimidating presence.",
  "该面具表现历史、小说或民间戏曲中的武将人物，通常用于突出忠勇、威严或护卫性的角色身份。": "This mask portrays a military figure from history, fiction or folk drama, emphasizing loyalty, courage, authority or a protective role.",
  "铁拐李又称“李铁拐”“铁拐先生”，为道教八仙中资历最老的神仙。据《历代神仙通鉴》卷五与《列仙全传》卷一等道经记载，铁拐李蓬头虬髯，巨眼坦腹踱足，模样丑恶，金箍束发，铁拐踱足，常背一药葫芦，浪迹江湖，行医治病，后功行圆满，被玉皇大帝封为上仙。": "Tieguai Li, also called Li Tieguai or Master Iron Crutch, is described as the most senior of the Daoist Eight Immortals. Daoist accounts including the Comprehensive Mirror of Immortals through the Ages and Complete Biographies of Immortals portray him with tangled hair, a curled beard, large eyes, a bare belly, a gold hair band and an iron crutch. Carrying a medicine gourd, he wanders and heals the sick. After perfecting his deeds and practice, he is appointed a high immortal by the Jade Emperor.",
  "清傩戏“领兵土地面具。该面具对应民间信仰中的神祇角色，多与护佑地方、祈福禳灾、风雨收成或仪式迎神有关。": "Qing-period Nuo mask of Tudi Leading the Troops. It represents a deity in popular religion, associated with protecting a locality, seeking blessings, averting misfortune, rain and harvests, or welcoming deities in ritual.",
  "白鹤童子，南极仙翁弟子，《白蛇传》中的鼓子曲《盗灵芝》唱道“白蛇女，上仙山，去盗灵芝。盗来了灵芝，下了山。白鹤童子拦住路，二人山下排战端。”。": "The White Crane Boy is a disciple of the Old Immortal of the South Pole. In the drum-song episode Stealing the Lingzhi from The Legend of the White Snake, White Snake climbs the immortal mountain to take the healing herb. On her descent, the White Crane Boy blocks her path and the two fight at the foot of the mountain.",
  "东汉末年名将。民间信仰：民间所供奉的“关公又被台湾信徒称为“恩主”，即救世主的意思。在东南亚地区，日本、新加坡、马来西亚以及菲律宾等国家，甚至美国、英国的华人区域，关公的信仰也都相当盛行，华侨在国外从商者很多，因此对于作为武财神的关公也多加崇祀。": "A celebrated general of the late Eastern Han. In popular belief, Guan Gong is also called Enzhu, or beneficent savior, by worshipers in Taiwan. His worship is widespread in Japan, Singapore, Malaysia, the Philippines and Chinese communities in the United States, Britain and elsewhere. Many overseas Chinese merchants honor him as a Martial God of Wealth.",
  "相传他身材魁梧、黑面虬髯是典型的关西大汉形象，初投黄巾军，关羽千里寻兄之时请求跟随，自此一直到死追随关羽；在听说关羽兵败被杀后，周仓更是自刎而死。在《三国演义》及此后的各种民间传说中，周仓均以关羽护卫的形象出现，在我国民间以及世界各地华人区的关帝庙中，关羽神像的两侧也经常供奉周仓、关平（关羽之子）的神像，可谓是家喻户晓。(人物集) 民间信仰：在中国传统对关羽的民间宗教信仰里，周仓名叫“周大将军”，是关圣帝君的贴身侍卫。明神宗万历四十二年一六一四年被封为“威灵惠勇公”。": "Zhou Cang is traditionally portrayed as a tall, powerful man with a dark face and curled beard. He first joins the Yellow Turbans, then asks to follow Guan Yu during Guan's long journey to find his sworn brother and remains loyal until death. On hearing that Guan Yu has been defeated and killed, he takes his own life. Romance of the Three Kingdoms and later folk traditions depict him as Guan Yu's guard. Statues of Zhou Cang and Guan Ping, Guan Yu's son, often flank Guan Yu in temples in China and overseas Chinese communities. In popular religion he is called General Zhou, the close attendant of the Holy Emperor Guan. The entry records his 1614 title as Duke of Awe-Inspiring Power, Beneficence and Courage.",
  "于建安六年（201）奉曹操之命攻击与刘备联合的汝南贼龚都等人，兵败被刘备所杀。民间信仰：在苏州评话中，蔡阳被称为“刀祖宗”，实力非常强大。": "In 201, Cai Yang was ordered by Cao Cao to attack Gong Du and others in Runan who had allied with Liu Bei. He was defeated and killed by Liu Bei. In Suzhou storytelling, he is known as the Ancestor of the Saber and is portrayed as exceptionally powerful.",
  "展出的清代三元大帝中的上元真君唐宏，面具体型庞大，两边有耳翅。": "Tang Hong, Lord of the Upper Origin among the Three Primordial Emperors, shown in a Qing-period mask. The mask is large, with wing-like extensions at both sides.",
  "面相凶恶的“狮头傩面具。该面具带有兽形、驱邪或原始祭仪意味，常通过夸张的口鼻、眼部和轮廓表现威慑力。": "A fierce Lion Head Nuo mask. It evokes animal forms, exorcism or early ritual practice. Exaggerated mouths, noses, eyes and outlines create an intimidating presence.",
  "文昌即文昌星，古时认为是主持文运功名的星宿。历朝历代的帝王对文昌帝君十分尊奉。历史上，文人士子，儒、佛、道都十分崇拜张亚子，还借文昌帝君之名，降写了大量著述，据不完全统计达80余部，数百种之多。这些经语中许多是劝善勉学的诗章。": "Wenchang refers to the Wenchang stars, traditionally believed to govern literary achievement and examination success. Emperors honored Wenchang Dijun across successive dynasties. Scholars and followers of Confucianism, Buddhism and Daoism revered Zhang Yazi. Numerous writings were produced in Wenchang's name; the entry cites an incomplete count of more than eighty works in hundreds of versions, many encouraging good conduct and study.",
  "土主剑阁杨村傩戏面具。该面具为未明确地区傩戏或傩仪中的角色面具，主要用于仪式表演、迎神还愿或民间信仰叙事。": "Tuzhu, a Nuo drama mask from Yangcun, Jiange. The entry also categorizes it as a character mask from an unspecified region, used in ritual performance, welcoming deities, fulfilling vows or narratives of popular belief.",
  "药王剑阁杨村傩戏面具药王是孙思邈,孙思邈世称孙真人,是唐代的医药学家、道士,精于内科,而且擅长妇科、儿科、外科、五官科,还著有《千金方》、《千金要方》、《千金翼方》。": "Yaowang, a Nuo drama mask from Yangcun, Jiange. The Medicine King is identified as Sun Simiao, also called Perfected Sun, a Tang physician and Daoist skilled in internal medicine, gynecology, pediatrics, surgery and treatment of the sense organs. His writings include the Qianjin Fang, Essential Prescriptions Worth a Thousand Gold Pieces and Supplementary Prescriptions Worth a Thousand Gold Pieces.",
  "灵官剑阁杨村傩戏面具道教有五百灵官的说法。其中最有名的“王灵官”，很多道家宫观的第一各大殿中，镇守道观山门的灵官一般都是这位王灵官。": "Lingguan, a Nuo drama mask from Yangcun, Jiange. Daoism speaks of five hundred divine officers, of whom Wang Lingguan is the best known. The guardian in the first hall of many Daoist temples is this Wang Lingguan, protecting the temple entrance.",
  "天门土地剑阁杨村傩戏面具秦汉以后为民俗广泛祀奉。在道教神系中地位较低，但在民间信仰极为普遍，是民间信仰中的地方保护神。": "Tianmen Tudi, a Nuo drama mask from Yangcun, Jiange. Worship of the local Earth God became widespread after the Qin and Han periods. Although relatively low in the Daoist hierarchy, he is extremely common in popular religion as the protector of a local community.",
  "笑和尚“剑阁杨村傩戏面具。该面具表现佛教人物或僧侣形象，常用于呈现慈和、诙谐或劝善意味的角色。": "Laughing Monk, a Nuo drama mask from Yangcun, Jiange. This mask portrays a Buddhist figure or monk, often conveying kindness, humor or encouragement to act well.",
  "和事老“剑阁杨村傩戏面具。该面具为未明确地区傩戏或傩仪中的角色面具，主要用于仪式表演、迎神还愿或民间信仰叙事。": "The Peacemaker, a Nuo drama mask from Yangcun, Jiange. The entry also categorizes it as a character mask from an unspecified region, used in ritual performance, welcoming deities, fulfilling vows or narratives of popular belief.",
  "雷公“剑阁杨村傩戏面具古代神话传说中的司雷之神，道教奉之为施行雷法的役使神。传说雷公和电母是一对夫妻。雷公名始见《楚辞》，因雷为天庭阳气，故称「公」。": "Leigong, a Nuo drama mask from Yangcun, Jiange. In traditional mythology he is the thunder deity; Daoism treats him as a divine agent of thunder rites. Legend describes Leigong and Dianmu as husband and wife. His name appears in the Songs of Chu; the masculine title Gong is explained through thunder's association with the heavenly yang force.",
  "梅花小姐“剑阁杨村傩戏面具。该面具表现傩仪中的女性神灵、祖先或家族护佑角色，常与求子、婚育、还愿和祈福主题相关。": "Miss Plum Blossom, a Nuo drama mask from Yangcun, Jiange. This mask represents a female deity, ancestor or family guardian in Nuo ritual, often associated with fertility, marriage, fulfilling vows and seeking blessings.",
  "五虎将 剑阁杨村傩戏面具分别为关羽、张飞、赵云、马超、黄忠。": "The Five Tiger Generals, Nuo drama masks from Yangcun, Jiange: Guan Yu, Zhang Fei, Zhao Yun, Ma Chao and Huang Zhong.",
  "收集整理大量的傩戏面具，傩面具作为傩戏这一非物质文化的载体之一，始终贯穿于傩戏发展过程中。人物傩面具颜色是一种象征面具人物品质，它本身就是一种造型艺术！": "A collection of Nuo drama masks. As one of the material carriers of this intangible heritage, masks have accompanied the development of Nuo drama. The entry presents the colors of character masks as symbolic of personal qualities and as a form of visual art.",
  "奶傩爸傩是苗族洪水神话中的兄妹两人，即傩公傩母或傩公傩娘，有的地方称“东山老人、南山小妹”，有的地方称“盘哥与瓠妹”。": "Nainuo and Banuo are the brother and sister in Miao flood mythology, also called Nuo Gong and Nuo Mu or Nuo Gong and Nuo Niang. Some places call them the Old Man of East Mountain and Little Sister of South Mountain, or Brother Pan and Sister Hu.",
  "傩公傩母为苗族信奉傩神！傩公傩母是我国南方众多民族傩坛中供奉的主神,傩公傩母神话则是广泛流传于我国西南各民族中的一则洪水神话，它与傩文化有着非常紧密的联系。": "Nuo Gong and Nuo Mu are Nuo deities worshiped by the Miao and principal deities at the Nuo altars of many communities in southern China. Their story is a flood myth widely shared among ethnic groups in the southwest and closely connected with Nuo culture.",
  "祁门傩面具大多以桃木、杨柳木、香樟木为原料，采用浅浮雕与镂空雕相结合，有后羿、魁星、李斯、夜叉、小鬼、老鼠精等60多种彩绘木雕面具，工艺精致，手法夸张，神气活现，其忠奸优劣、老少妍陋无不神似。": "Qimen Nuo masks are mostly carved from peachwood, willow or camphorwood, combining shallow relief and pierced carving. More than sixty painted wooden types include Hou Yi, Kuixing, Li Si, Yaksha, Little Ghost and Rat Spirit. Their detailed, exaggerated forms vividly distinguish loyalty and treachery, excellence and baseness, youth and age, beauty and ugliness.",
  "南坑车湘傩舞中太子的面具。该面具为未明确地区傩戏或傩仪中的角色面具，主要用于仪式表演、迎神还愿或民间信仰叙事。": "The Crown Prince mask from the Nankeng Chexiang Nuo dance. The entry also categorizes it as a character mask from an unspecified region, used in ritual performance, welcoming deities, fulfilling vows or narratives of popular belief.",
  "图文作者：项智洪。该面具为未明确地区傩戏或傩仪中的角色面具，主要用于仪式表演、迎神还愿或民间信仰叙事。": "Text and images by Xiang Zhihong. This is a character mask associated with Nuo drama or ritual from an unspecified region, used in ritual performance, welcoming deities, fulfilling vows or narratives of popular belief.",
  "梅山傩是古老的中国傩文化体系中一朵丰标独树的奇葩。梅山傩面具叶具有独特的艺术欣赏性。田彦拍摄。": "Meishan Nuo is a distinctive branch of China's longstanding Nuo traditions. Its masks also have their own artistic qualities. Photograph by Tian Yan.",
  "杨村傩戏面具 山王、歪嘴、莫下巴... 多数情况下由一人游走演唱，表演者戴没有下颚的面具，手拿小马锣身背红布褡裢，褡裢中装桃木和蓑草，乾坤独步、走唱游吟。": "Yangcun Nuo drama masks: Mountain King, Crooked Mouth, No Chin and others. Performances are often given by a single traveling singer wearing a mask without a lower jaw, carrying a small gong and a red cloth shoulder bag containing peachwood and coir grass, moving and singing alone.",
  "龙须吞口作为民间常见的民俗作品，这样的造型极为少见。吞口是云、贵、川、湘等省一些少数民族地区挂在门楣上，用于驱邪的木雕，大多以兽头为主，也有人兽结合的，还有挂葫芦或木瓢的。": "Dragon-Whiskered Tunkou. Although tunkou are common folk objects, this particular form is unusual. These protective wooden carvings are hung above doorways in some minority communities in Yunnan, Guizhou, Sichuan and Hunan. Most resemble animal heads, while others combine human and animal features or use gourds or wooden ladles.",
  "甘肃陇南白马藏族的十二相，由狮子、牛、虎、龙、鸡、猪六个生肖动物、两个“池哥”、两个“池母和两个“笑面小鬼组成。而阿坝南坪白马人“麻昼中的“十二生肖为：龙、牛、虎、豹、熊、狮子、凤凰、羊、大鬼、小鬼、男鬼、女鬼。正是唐代敦煌民间“十二属驱傩的遗迹。龙、凤、虎、熊、豹，有原始图腾崇拜的痕迹，牛、羊打上了农耕畜牧的烙印，而大小鬼、男女鬼极富世俗色彩，这种十二相的杂糅，非常符合明清时期民间傩的特征。": "The Twelve Forms of the Baima Tibetan communities in Longnan, Gansu, comprise six animals—lion, ox, tiger, dragon, rooster and pig—plus two Chige, two Chimu and two smiling Little Ghosts. The Twelve Zodiac figures in the Baima Mazhou tradition of Nanping, Aba, instead include dragon, ox, tiger, leopard, bear, lion, phoenix, sheep, Great Ghost, Little Ghost, Male Ghost and Female Ghost. The entry interprets them as remnants of the twelve-animal exorcistic traditions of Tang-period Dunhuang. It associates dragons, phoenixes, tigers, bears and leopards with early totemic worship, oxen and sheep with farming and herding, and the various ghosts with worldly life, describing this mixture as characteristic of popular Nuo in the Ming and Qing periods.",
  "十二生肖，又叫属相，是中国与十二地支相配以人出生年份的十二种动物，包括鼠、牛、虎、兔、龙、蛇、马、羊、猴、鸡、狗、猪。作者：庄迅 作品名称：十二生肖 材质：泡桐 天文学与历法 十二生肖与古代中国的天干地支纪年法密切相关。地支共有十二个，分别为子、丑、寅、卯、辰、巳、午、未、申、酉、戌、亥。为便于记忆，古人用十二种动物代表地支，形成十二生肖，即鼠、牛、虎、兔、龙、蛇、马、羊、猴、鸡、狗、猪。动物崇拜 古代中国有动物崇拜传统，许多动物被视为神灵或象征，如龙象征权力，虎象征勇猛。十二生肖中的动物大多与人类生活密切相关，反映了古人对自然的观察与崇拜。民间传说 关于十二生肖的排列顺序，有多种民间传说。例如，传说当年轩辕黄帝要选十二动物担任宫廷卫士，老鼠因为使用计谋得了第一名，牛排第二，虎和龙被封为山神和海神，排在牛的后面，最后形成了鼠、牛、虎、兔、龙、蛇、马、羊、猴、鸡、狗、猪的顺序。": "The Chinese zodiac associates twelve animals with the twelve Earthly Branches and a person's birth year: rat, ox, tiger, rabbit, dragon, snake, horse, sheep, monkey, rooster, dog and pig. Artist: Zhuang Xun. Title: Twelve Zodiac Animals. Material: paulownia wood. Astronomy and calendar: the zodiac is closely connected to the traditional Heavenly Stems and Earthly Branches calendar. The branches are Zi, Chou, Yin, Mao, Chen, Si, Wu, Wei, Shen, You, Xu and Hai; animals make them easier to remember. Animal worship: traditional Chinese culture treated many animals as divine or symbolic, with the dragon associated with power and the tiger with courage. Most zodiac animals were close to everyday life, reflecting observation and reverence for nature. Folk legends offer different explanations for their order. In one, the Yellow Emperor selects twelve palace guards; the rat wins first place through a trick, the ox comes second, and the tiger and dragon become mountain and sea deities behind it, producing the familiar sequence."
});
